```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My Joke Website</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            text-align: center;
            background-color: #f0f0f0;
            padding: 50px;
        }
        .container {
            border: 2px solid #333;
            border-radius: 10px;
            background-color: #fff;
            padding: 20px;
            box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
        }
        h1 {
            color: #333;
        }
        .joke-box {
            margin: 20px 0;
        }
        button {
            padding: 10px 20px;
            font-size: 16px;
            background-color: #2ecc71;
            color: white;
            border: none;
            border-radius: 5px;
            cursor: pointer;
        }
        button:hover {
            background-color: #27ae60;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <h1>My Joke Website</h1>
        <div class="joke-box">
            <div id="joke">[Funny Joke]</div>
            <button onclick="revealJoke()">Push to reveal punchline</button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <script>
        const joke = "Why don't scientists trust atoms? Because they make up everything!";
        document.getElementById("joke").textContent = joke;
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

This code creates a simple, colorful website with a joke that is revealed when a button is clicked. You can replace the joke text with any joke you like.
